  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSimple Interest for 4 2/5 years at 7.6% = 8,778\n\nTime1 = 4(2)/(5) = 22/5 years\n\nRate1 = 7.6%\n\nRate2 = 4.8%\n\nTime2 = 8(2)/(7) = 58/7 years\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSimple Interest = (P × R × T) ÷ 100\n\nAmount = Principal + Simple Interest\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ SI1 = (P × 7.6 × 22/5) ÷ 100 = 8,778\n\n⇒ P × 7.6 × 22/5 = 8,778 × 100\n\n⇒ P × 7.6 × 22/5 = 8,77,800\n\n⇒ P × 7.6 × 22 = 8,77,800 × 5\n\n⇒ P × 167.2 = 43,89,000\n\n⇒ P = 43,89,000 ÷ 167.2\n\n⇒ P = 26,250\n\n \n\n**Now find SI at 4.8% for 58/7 years:**\n\n⇒ SI2 = (26,250 × 4.8 × 58/7) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ SI2 = 26,250 × 0.048 × 58/7\n\n⇒ SI2 = 1,260 × 58/7\n\n⇒ SI2 = 180 × 58\n\n⇒ SI2 = 10,440\n\n \n\n**Amount payable = Principal + SI2**\n\n⇒ Amount = 26,250 + 10,440\n\n⇒ Amount = 36,690\n\n**∴ The amount payable is 36,690.**",
